trong Barrett closing argument with national Republican surrogates could tighten this into a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District is one of the most competitive House races of 2026, with first-term Republican Tom Barrett defending an even-PVI seat against Democrat William Lawrence. The contest has drawn enormous outside spending, making it the nation's most expensive House ad race, and both campaigns have sought to distance themselves from national party extremes. Vice President JD Vance has campaigned for Barrett while Lawrence has appeared with Governor Whitmer.\n\nPrediction markets price Lawrence's win chances around 76%, and most late-October expert ratings call the race Lean D or a likely flip, though Cook, Inside Elections, and Sabato still rate it a Tossup. The only recent independent poll, from Emerson in mid-October, showed Lawrence ahead by 8. The forecast lands at a modest Democratic edge with elevated uncertainty, reflecting thin polling and Barrett's incumbency advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin":